+# Implementation Plan: JSON Pointer Resolution
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md) | **Constitution**: unfilled template, no rules to check.
+
+## Technical Context
+TypeScript (ES2022, NodeNext, strict), no runtime dependencies, tests with `node:test`
+(`npm test`, Node 22 runs `.ts` via type stripping).
+
+## Structure
+- `src/pointer.ts` — `resolvePointer`, parse/unescape helpers
+- `src/index.ts` — re-exports `resolvePointer`
+- `test/pointer.test.ts` — RFC examples + error cases
+
+## Design
+Validate string and leading `/`; split on `/`; validate `~` escapes with `/~(?![01])/`; unescape `~1` then `~0`.
+Walk tokens: arrays need `/^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$/` and index < length; objects use `Object.hasOwn`; anything else throws.
